    "answer": {
      "short": "$(a,n)=(1,55),(7,13),(49,7)$.\n\nComparing the two coefficients gives $a(n-6)=49$.",
      "worked": "Let $C_6$ and $C_7$ be the coefficients of $x^6$ and $x^7$ respectively. Both are non-zero, so $n\\geq7$ and $a\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}C_6&=\\binom{n}{6}5^{n-6}a^6\\\\C_7&=\\binom{n}{7}5^{n-7}a^7\\\\\\frac{C_6}{C_7}&=\\frac{\\binom{n}{6}}{\\binom{n}{7}}\\frac{5}{a}\\\\\\frac{C_6}{C_7}&=\\frac{35}{a(n-6)}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the given ratio,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{35}{a(n-6)}&=\\frac{5}{7}\\\\a(n-6)&=49.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n-6$ is a positive integer, $a$ is a positive integer divisor of $49$. The factor pairs $(a,n-6)$ are $(1,49),(7,7),(49,1)$.\nThus $(a,n)=(1,55),(7,13),(49,7)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
